  "description": "DAPDOP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H210 Co6 Dy8 O60 P6,3.5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5? (Dy) has 0 O neighbors; Co5? (Co) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.182-3.986 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.26-119.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoII6DyIII8(μ3-OH)8(O3P tBu)6(O2C tBu)16(H2O)2](MeCN)y (x = 0, y = 2). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
